If you're labeling the jump in your cash balance chart caused by a stock redemption, merger payout, or delisted position cash settlement, common names are:
Payout
Cash Payout
Redemption Payout
Settlement Credit
Cash Distribution
Corporate Action Payout
Liquidation Proceeds
Merger Consideration
Position Redemption
Delisting Settlement
For the chart shown, a concise transaction label would be:
Payout Fee (if a fee was charged)
Payout (if cash was received)
Payout Credit (if cash was added to the account)
Redemption Payout (if the SPAC/share was redeemed)
Since PSPC was delisted and your cash balance increased from approximately $0 to $16.97, "Redemption Payout" or "Cash Payout" would be the most accurate labels.
